    "reason": "THE PERIOD WALL'S PACKED-ROW INTERFACE — the thing the onset wall was given on 2026-09-10 and the period wall still lacks. The landed leftDiagonal_periodicFrom_of_rowNat_agree carries the hypothesis T ≤ 2k, because it is aimed at the ONSET wall and must land the onset at k. leftDiagonal_period_le does not care where the repetition starts, only how long its period is, so that hypothesis is pure friction there and this drops it. With this in hand, leftDiagonal_period_le reduces to a statement with no automaton in it: for every k there is some p ≤ k + 1 and some row T with rowNat T ≡ rowNat (T + p) mod 2^(k+1). That is the period wall in the one vocabulary the kernel can compute in — rowNat reaches row 5000 in a second where evolve gives out near row 18 — and unlike the onset ladder's constant it carries no expiry: crystal 57 shows the onset route's constant 16 dies at k = 87867 because it is fixed, while here p is allowed to grow with k and the truth is about 2·log2(k), so the margin widens rather than closing. Cited by any period-wall argument that wants to work on rows instead of diagonals, and it is the companion to the closed leftDiagonal_period_le_of_white_count, which reduces the same wall to a count of eventually-white diagonals — two independent handles on one wall rather than one.",
